00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:47.710
He had to start a whole new company.
他得开创一家全新的公司。

274
00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:50.270
He had to, like, establish Saber.
他得，就像是，建立起赛博公司。

275
00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:54.210
Well, it's a big episode to make your directorial debut, my lord.
天呐，作为导演处女作，这一集的分量可真重。

276
00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:56.770
Well, John talked a little bit about it.
嗯，约翰谈到过一点。

277
00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:57.570
Here we go.
我们来看看。

278
00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:01.510
Introducing Kathy Bates, which was so mind-blowing.
引入凯西·贝茨，这太令人震撼了。

279
00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:07.050
The Kathy Bates was not only on our show, but I was her first experience as a director.
凯西·贝茨不仅出现在我们的节目中，而且我还是她作为导演的第一位合作对象。

280
00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:10.130
And for that, I will always be apologetic to her.
对于这一点，我永远都会向她表示歉意。

281
00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:17.950
But I remember introducing that character and knowing that, I don't know, feeling a big responsibility that that character was going to be a big part of the show.
但我记得在引入那个角色时，我感到一种巨大的责任感，因为那个角色将成为剧中的重要组成部分。

282
00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:28.190
And bringing along with her was Zach Woods, who I remember from the moment we shot his first stuff, the whole water bottle storyline.
随她而来的是扎克·伍兹，我记得从我们拍摄他第一场戏，也就是那个水瓶剧情开始。

283
00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:31.430
He was just so unbelievably funny.
他就好笑得不可思议。

284
00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:38.410
He was so reserved in this brand-new instrument that we had to play with on the show, a totally different character than anybody else.
他表现得非常内敛，是我们剧中一个全新的表演工具，是一个与众不同的角色。

285
00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:42.850
And yet, whenever he spoke, you couldn't take your eyes off of him.
然而，每当他开口，你就无法将目光从他身上移开。

286
00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.850
He was always so, so funny.
他总是那么那么好笑。

287
00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:52.770
And I just remember with the big story changes that were happening in the show, I was so nervous to be the one to introduce those two characters.
我只记得当时剧集发生了巨大的剧情变动，作为引入这两个角色的人，我感到非常紧张。

288
00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:57.470
And then in the end, I don't know, feel somewhat honored to have been a part of it.
但最后，我不知道，能参与其中还是感到有些荣幸。

289
00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.670
I think those guys were lucky to have John as a director.
我觉得那些人能有约翰当导演真是幸运。

290
00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.270
He's so personable.
他非常平易近人。

291
00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:03.710
He puts you so at ease.
他让你感到非常放松。

292
00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:07.770
I mean, listen, all of our directors have a place in my heart.
我是说，听着，我们所有的导演在我心中都占有一席之地。

293
00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:08.570
They're all great.
他们都很棒。

294
00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:16.090
But John really does have a gift at, like, walking into a room and just putting everyone, like, out of their heads.
但约翰确实有一种天赋，走进一个房间就能让每个人放下心理负担。

295
00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:16.930
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

296
00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:17.990
He's a good connector.
他很擅长建立人际连接。

297
00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:18.390
He is.
确实。

298
00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:19.150
He's good at connecting.
他很擅长建立连接。

299
00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:19.650
Yeah.
是啊。

300
00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:20.210
Instantly.
瞬间就能做到。

301
00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:21.750
All right, Angela.
好了，安吉拉。

