Well, remember years ago when we found out that you could hack someone's camera in their
还记得几年前我们发现可以黑进别人电脑的摄像头吗？

1086
00:48:54.110 --> 00:48:54.930
computer?
电脑？

1087
00:48:55.210 --> 00:48:58.350
And so, then we started putting Post-it notes over our cameras.
所以后来我们开始在摄像头上贴便利贴。

1088
00:48:58.410 --> 00:48:59.250
Over our camera.
贴在摄像头上。

1089
00:48:59.430 --> 00:48:59.650
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1090
00:48:59.950 --> 00:49:00.510
I know.
我知道。

1091
00:49:00.610 --> 00:49:01.810
Everyone, you should do that.
大家，你们都应该这么做。

1092
00:49:01.950 --> 00:49:04.810
You should put a Post-it note over the little camera in your computer.
你应该在电脑的小摄像头上贴一张便利贴。

1093
00:49:04.950 --> 00:49:05.130
Right.
没错。

1094
00:49:05.150 --> 00:49:06.630
Or a piece of tape or what have you.
或者贴块胶带什么的。

1095
00:49:06.670 --> 00:49:10.530
Yes, because we read that article where you can hack into it.
是的，因为我们读过那篇关于可以黑进摄像头的文章。

1096
00:49:10.730 --> 00:49:10.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1097
00:49:10.950 --> 00:49:14.130
And then people just watch you in your house.
然后人们就能在家里看着你。

1098
00:49:14.310 --> 00:49:14.930
How creepy.
太毛骨悚然了。

1099
00:49:15.370 --> 00:49:16.270
It's creepskis.
简直是变态。

1100
00:49:16.570 --> 00:49:17.630
Super creeper.
超级变态。

1101
00:49:18.330 --> 00:49:18.630
All right.
好的。

1102
00:49:18.810 --> 00:49:20.410
So, back to the conference room.
那么，回到会议室。

1103
00:49:20.490 --> 00:49:20.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1104
00:49:21.350 --> 00:49:22.810
Gabe has shown the video.
盖博展示了视频。

1105
00:49:23.050 --> 00:49:24.630
People are digesting it.
大家正在消化内容。

1106
00:49:25.070 --> 00:49:28.390
Jim has a sarcastic talking head about it.
吉姆对此发表了一段讽刺的采访。

1107
00:49:28.490 --> 00:49:30.790
With a great impression by John Krasinski.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基模仿得太棒了。

1108
00:49:31.070 --> 00:49:31.730
Very good.
非常好。

1109
00:49:31.910 --> 00:49:33.410
Well, you know he's good at the impressions.
嗯，你知道他很擅长模仿。

1110
00:49:33.790 --> 00:49:34.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1111
00:49:34.050 --> 00:49:38.870
Well, now Gabe is going to explain that Saber primarily sells printers.
现在盖博要解释说，赛博公司主要卖的是打印机。

1112
00:49:39.290 --> 00:49:45.830
So, he wants everybody to consider themselves printer salesmen who also sell paper.
所以，他希望每个人都把自己看作是卖打印机的，顺便也卖纸。

1113
00:49:46.190 --> 00:49:47.510
Michael doesn't like this.
迈克尔不喜欢这样。

1114
00:49:47.610 --> 00:49:48.830
He doesn't care for it.
他对此很不感冒。

1115
00:49:48.870 --> 00:49:50.530
It's about to get worse for Michael, though.
不过，迈克尔的处境还要变得更糟。

1116
00:49:51.150 --> 00:49:53.870
Gabe then starts going over all the new company policies.
接着盖博开始逐一讲解公司的新政策。

1117
00:49:54.270 --> 00:49:57.130
At 6 minutes, 58 seconds, Meredith yells,
在6分58秒时，梅雷迪斯大喊道：

1118
00:49:57.370 --> 00:49:58.890
Talk about vacation days!
说说休假天数的事儿！

1119
00:49:59.310 --> 00:50:01.430
Such an, like, odd heckle from Meredith.
梅雷迪斯的插话真是……挺奇怪的。

1120
00:50:02.070 --> 00:50:07.790
Meredith, this was a much longer scene where everyone shares about their vacation days.
梅雷迪斯，这原本是一场很长的戏，大家都在分享自己的休假天数。

1121
00:50:08.070 --> 00:50:09.470
And, Jenna, it just cracked me up.
而且，珍娜，那段真的把我逗乐了。

1122
00:50:09.550 --> 00:50:10.750
I want to share a little bit with you.
我想和你们分享一点点。

1123
00:50:11.190 --> 00:50:12.050
Meredith says,
梅雷迪斯说：

1124
00:50:12.250 --> 00:50:13.750
I saved up days from last year.
我攒了去年的假期。

1125
00:50:13.790 --> 00:50:15.170
I want to go to Jamaica.
我想去牙买加。

1126
00:50:15.170 --> 00:50:18.110
And then she stands up, rolls her hips, and says,
然后她站起来，扭动着臀部说：

1127
00:50:18.470 --> 00:50:20.430
How Meredith got her groove back.
梅雷迪斯如何找回她的风采。

1128
00:50:20.810 --> 00:50:21.150
Okay.
好的。

1129
00:50:21.470 --> 00:50:21.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1130
00:50:22.330 --> 00:50:24.370
Stanley has a talking head where he says,
斯坦利有一段采访，他说：

1131
00:50:24.530 --> 00:50:26.130
I need those vacation days.
我需要那些休假天数。

1132
00:50:26.130 --> 00:50:27.090
I have two women.
我有两个女人。

1133
00:50:27.290 --> 00:50:30.130
One likes to ski, and one likes the tropics.
一个喜欢滑雪，一个喜欢热带。

1134
00:50:30.130 --> 00:50:31.230
It's very difficult.
这太难了。

1135
00:50:31.430 --> 00:50:34.270
But I am not complaining or asking to be judged.
但我不是在抱怨，也不是在请求评判。

1136
00:50:34.470 --> 00:50:35.690
I just need some time off.
我只是需要一点时间休息。

1137
00:50:36.230 --> 00:50:36.570
Okay.
好的。

1138
00:50:37.370 --> 00:50:39.110
And then Michael says,
然后迈克尔说：

1139
00:50:39.710 --> 00:50:42.970
What if you've been saving up for days like a big trip in the future,
如果你为了未来的大旅行一直在攒假期怎么办，

1140
00:50:43.150 --> 00:50:45.070
like a 40-day family safari?
比如40天的家庭游猎之旅？

1141
00:50:45.890 --> 00:50:46.810
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

1142
00:50:47.050 --> 00:50:47.490
Gabe says,
盖博说：

1143
00:50:47.590 --> 00:50:52.430
I'm sorry, but maybe you could look into a two-week safari for your family.
抱歉，但也许你可以考虑给你的家人安排两周的游猎之旅。

1144
00:50:52.870 --> 00:50:53.910
And Michael says,
迈克尔说：

1145
00:50:54.030 --> 00:50:57.010
You can't take 12 kids on a safari in only two weeks.
你不可能在两周内带12个孩子去游猎。

1146
00:50:57.250 --> 00:50:58.530
And Stanley says,
斯坦利说：

1147
00:50:58.670 --> 00:51:00.270
You can if they're imaginary.
如果他们是虚构的，那就可以。

1148
00:51:00.270 --> 00:51:02.190
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1149
00:51:02.470 --> 00:51:09.490
And then Kelly explains she actually owes the company days because she tried out for American Idol and took time off.
然后凯利解释说，她实际上还欠公司天数，因为她去参加了《美国偶像》的选拔，请了假。

1150
00:51:09.610 --> 00:51:13.630
She went to Atlanta, Boston, and Cincinnati, and she did not advance.
她去了亚特兰大、波士顿和辛辛那提，但没能晋级。

1151
00:51:14.390 --> 00:51:15.390
These are amazing.
这些太棒了。

1152
00:51:15.390 --> 00:51:15.910
I know.
我知道。

1153
00:51:16.070 --> 00:51:18.050
But here's my favorite part.
但这是我最喜欢的部分。

1154
00:51:18.330 --> 00:51:22.710
This scene would have ended with a line from Creed, and I am so bummed it got cut.
这一幕本该有一句克里德的台词，被删掉我真的很遗憾。

1155
00:51:23.030 --> 00:51:27.610
While they're talking about their vacation time and whether it will roll over or not for Saber,
当他们在讨论假期时间以及是否能结转到赛博公司时，

1156
00:51:28.410 --> 00:51:30.950
Meredith sees the IT guy, right?
梅雷迪思看到了IT小哥，对吧？

1157
00:51:31.170 --> 00:51:31.510
Yes.
是的。

1158
00:51:31.510 --> 00:51:32.230
And she says,
然后她说，

1159
00:51:32.610 --> 00:51:34.670
Hey, who the hell's going through our stuff?
嘿，到底是谁在翻我们的东西？

1160
00:51:35.010 --> 00:51:36.310
And Creed says,
克里德说，

1161
00:51:36.850 --> 00:51:38.030
Oh, that's just Sam.
哦，那是萨姆。

1162
00:51:38.190 --> 00:51:38.970
He's with me.
他跟我一起的。

1163
00:51:39.750 --> 00:51:40.270
What?
什么？

1164
00:51:41.290 --> 00:51:42.570
And then Gabe goes,
然后盖博说，

1165
00:51:42.770 --> 00:51:45.190
Actually, that's Nick, your new IT guy.
其实那是尼克，你们新的IT人员。

1166
00:51:45.350 --> 00:51:47.230
And then the scene progresses as aired.
然后剧情就按播出的那样发展了。

1167
00:51:47.230 --> 00:51:49.910
But I just love that Creed thought he knew this guy.
但我就是喜欢克里德以为他认识那个人。

1168
00:51:50.070 --> 00:51:50.330
He's like,
他说，

1169
00:51:50.390 --> 00:51:50.970
Oh, that's Sam.
哦，那是萨姆。

1170
00:51:51.170 --> 00:51:52.010
He's with me.
他跟我一起的。

1171
00:51:52.330 --> 00:51:55.290
Well, here is something that a lot of people flagged.
好吧，这里有很多人指出的一个点。

1172
00:51:55.510 --> 00:51:59.550
When we cut over to Nick, the new IT guy,
当我们切到新来的IT人员尼克时，

1173
00:51:59.970 --> 00:52:09.210
many people noticed that it is the same person who was giving graphic design career advice to Pam at the job fair.
很多人注意到他就是之前在招聘会上给帕姆提供平面设计职业建议的那个人。

1174
00:52:09.210 --> 00:52:09.850
Yeah.
没错。

1175
00:52:10.130 --> 00:52:12.790
I asked Randy about this, and he said,
我问了兰迪这件事，他说，

1176
00:52:12.930 --> 00:52:15.930
Well, now, job fair was not on his watch,
嗯，招聘会那集不是他负责的，

1177
00:52:15.930 --> 00:52:21.430
but he did remember that a lot of the writers really, really loved this actor,
但他记得很多编剧真的非常非常喜欢这个演员，

1178
00:52:21.650 --> 00:52:25.950
who, by the way, Nelson Franklin, who previously appeared in job fair.
顺便说一下，他叫尼尔森·富兰克林，之前在招聘会那集出现过。

1179
00:52:26.170 --> 00:52:27.370
And they just decided,
他们就决定，

1180
00:52:27.610 --> 00:52:28.210
We don't care.
我们不在乎。

1181
00:52:28.210 --> 00:52:30.470
We're going to bring him back because this is now an arc.
我们要让他回来，因为这现在是一个系列剧情了。

1182
00:52:30.630 --> 00:52:33.210
He's going to appear in four episodes as Nick.
他会以尼克的身份出演四集。

1183
00:52:33.790 --> 00:52:35.790
He's really an amazing comedic actor.
他真的是一位了不起的喜剧演员。

1184
00:52:36.290 --> 00:52:39.770
You've probably seen him on Black-ish, Veep, Arrested Development.
你可能在《黑人一家亲》、《副总统》、《发展受阻》里见过他。

1185
00:52:40.010 --> 00:52:43.390
And Angela, you know him because you guys were both on Black AF together.
安吉拉，你认识他，因为你们俩都演过《黑人一家亲》。

1186
00:52:43.590 --> 00:52:44.210
We were.
我们确实演过。

1187
00:52:44.430 --> 00:52:46.970
It was just the craziest little office reunion.
那简直是一场疯狂的办公室重聚。

1188
00:52:47.210 --> 00:52:48.890
Ken Quapis directed our episode.
肯·夸皮斯执导了我们那一集。

1189
00:52:49.390 --> 00:52:52.310
Nelson and I played writers in a writer's room.
尼尔森和我在编剧室里演编剧。

1190
00:52:52.470 --> 00:52:53.510
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1191
00:52:53.650 --> 00:52:54.230
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1192
00:52:54.370 --> 00:52:56.490
And then Rashida plays Kenya's wife.
然后拉什达演肯尼亚的妻子。

1193
00:52:56.490 --> 00:52:58.670
And we all were there on the same day.
我们那天都在现场。

1194
00:52:59.010 --> 00:53:00.110
Well, we had a blaSt.
我们玩得很开心。

1195
00:53:00.250 --> 00:53:00.950
Nelson's great.
尼尔森很棒。

1196
00:53:01.070 --> 00:53:02.570
I was excited he got to come back.
他能回来我很高兴。

1197
00:53:02.750 --> 00:53:03.210
Me too.
我也是。

1198
00:53:03.230 --> 00:53:04.350
I really liked him.
我真的很喜欢他。

1199
00:53:04.350 --> 00:53:12.310
His character is going through our computers and he's going to put up like blockers so that
他的角色正在检查我们的电脑，他打算设置一些拦截器，这样

1200
00:53:12.310 --> 00:53:15.530
we can't waste time on certain websites.
我们就不能在某些网站上浪费时间了。

1201
00:53:15.950 --> 00:53:19.490
I mean, when he says YouTube, it looked like Michael pooped himself a little.
我是说，当他说到YouTube时，迈克尔看起来像是吓得拉裤兜子了。

1202
00:53:19.710 --> 00:53:20.790
Very upset.
非常心烦。

1203
00:53:21.230 --> 00:53:23.190
But wait, there's more.
但等等，还有呢。

1204
00:53:23.390 --> 00:53:24.590
It doesn't stop there.
还没完呢。

1205
00:53:25.150 --> 00:53:27.830
Gabe has even more new policies.
盖博还有更多新政策。

1206
00:53:28.330 --> 00:53:30.870
But before we do that, I think we should take a break.
但在那之前，我觉得我们应该休息一下。

1207
00:53:31.010 --> 00:53:31.910
I need to use the restroom.
我得去趟洗手间。

1208
00:53:32.330 --> 00:53:32.930
Okay.
好的。

1209
00:53:33.830 --> 00:53:35.110
You're not going to argue with me.
你不会跟我争论这个的。

1210
00:53:35.210 --> 00:53:35.870
I appreciate it.
我很感激。

1211
00:53:35.930 --> 00:53:38.070
I will never argue with you for having to pee.
我绝不会因为你要上厕所而跟你争论。

1212
00:53:38.230 --> 00:53:39.190
You know this about me.
你了解我的。

1213
00:53:39.350 --> 00:53:41.330
It's one of our company policies.
这是我们公司的政策之一。

1214
00:53:41.670 --> 00:53:43.090
Pee whenever you need to.
想上厕所就去。

1215
00:53:43.190 --> 00:53:44.190
Go to the bathroom.
去洗手间吧。

1216
00:53:44.190 --> 00:53:44.870
You go to the bathroom.
你去洗手间吧。

1217
00:53:44.890 --> 00:53:45.430
That's right.
没错。

1218
00:53:56.660 --> 00:53:57.660
We are back.
我们回来了。

1219
00:53:58.040 --> 00:53:59.180
My bladder is empty.
我的膀胱排空了。

1220
00:53:59.520 --> 00:54:01.640
Your bladder is empty and I ate half a donut.
你的膀胱排空了，而我吃了一半甜甜圈。

1221
00:54:02.360 --> 00:54:03.840
So on brand for you, lady.
真符合你的风格，女士。

1222
00:54:04.440 --> 00:54:05.840
Someone brought donuts today.
今天有人带了甜甜圈来。

1223
00:54:06.060 --> 00:54:08.840
It was my happiest moment of my day so far.
这是我今天目前为止最开心的时刻。

1224
00:54:08.840 --> 00:54:10.120
But only half of it.
但只吃了一半。

1225
00:54:10.280 --> 00:54:11.660
You only ever eat half of anything.
你吃什么都只吃一半。

1226
00:54:11.980 --> 00:54:12.060
That's right.
没错。

1227
00:54:12.780 --> 00:54:19.220
Well, listen, Gabe is in the conference room and his next new announcement is that he is
听着，盖博在会议室里，他的下一个新公告是

1228
00:54:19.220 --> 00:54:23.520
going to give each employee an aluminum Sabre water bottle.
他要给每位员工发一个赛博铝制水瓶。

1229
00:54:23.520 --> 00:54:26.400
This is going to eliminate the need for plastic.
这将消除对塑料的需求。

1230
00:54:26.860 --> 00:54:28.780
It's going to be really good for the environment.
这对环境会非常有好处。

1231
00:54:29.940 --> 00:54:33.000
But Michael is like upset.
但迈克尔很不高兴。

1232
00:54:33.500 --> 00:54:35.660
He's like, what about my little cups?
他就像是说，那我那些小纸杯怎么办？

1233
00:54:35.800 --> 00:54:37.440
Like my little cups I drink the water out of.
就是我用来喝水的那种小纸杯。

1234
00:54:37.560 --> 00:54:39.060
He drinks 20 a day.
他一天要喝20杯。

1235
00:54:39.060 --> 00:54:41.840
Now, here's the thing that I think is kind of brilliant.
现在，我觉得有一点很绝。

1236
00:54:42.280 --> 00:54:47.280
Because Gabe says, I bet you can fit those 20 little cups into your water bottle.
因为盖博说，我打赌你可以把那20个小纸杯塞进你的水瓶里。

1237
00:54:47.720 --> 00:54:54.200
And Michael says, but what about the 20 little trips that I take to the water cooler each day
迈克尔说，那我每天去饮水机那20趟怎么办？

1238
00:54:54.200 --> 00:54:58.920
where he scans the office or his 20 little conversations with Stanley?
他去那儿扫视办公室，或者跟斯坦利那20次闲聊怎么办？

1239
00:54:59.200 --> 00:54:59.900
Poor Stanley.
可怜的斯坦利。

1240
00:55:00.160 --> 00:55:01.620
Stanley's like, I can let go.
斯坦利就像是说，我能放手了。

1241
00:55:01.760 --> 00:55:05.860
All this time, Stanley, like unbeknownst to us,
一直以来，斯坦利，我们竟然都不知道，

1242
00:55:05.860 --> 00:55:10.880
he's having 20 conversations a day with Michael because he sits by the water cooler.
他每天要跟迈克尔聊20次，因为他坐在饮水机旁边。

1243
00:55:11.220 --> 00:55:14.100
I'm surprised he hasn't moved the water cooler personally,
我很惊讶他竟然没亲自把饮水机搬走，

1244
00:55:14.100 --> 00:55:16.800
that Stanley didn't move it like back into the annex.
惊讶斯坦利没把它搬到附楼去。

1245
00:55:17.080 --> 00:55:20.440
I'm surprised Stanley hasn't requested to like trade seats with Creed.
我很惊讶斯坦利没申请跟克里德换座位。

1246
00:55:21.160 --> 00:55:21.600
Truly.
真的。

1247
00:55:22.340 --> 00:55:24.340
Well, he likes his relationship with Phyllis.
嗯，他喜欢他和菲利斯的关系。

1248
00:55:24.460 --> 00:55:25.040
We know that.
我们都知道。

1249
00:55:25.240 --> 00:55:26.280
That's his work wife.
那是他的职场老婆。

1250
00:55:26.840 --> 00:55:29.840
I just want to say, I think it's actually a little genius.
我只想说，我觉得这其实有点天才。

1251
00:55:30.220 --> 00:55:33.900
The trip to the water cooler as a managerial technique.
把去饮水机接水当成一种管理技巧。

1252
00:55:33.900 --> 00:55:36.000
I was like, oh, smart.
我当时心想，噢，真聪明。

1253
00:55:36.400 --> 00:55:39.800
If Michael really wanted to manage people, he just gets bored.
如果迈克尔真的想管理员工，他只会觉得无聊。

1254
00:55:40.140 --> 00:55:40.940
That's true.
确实如此。

1255
00:55:41.240 --> 00:55:43.380
Probably driven from another place.
大概是出于其他原因吧。

1256
00:55:43.760 --> 00:55:48.160
Well, at 7 minutes, 28 seconds, if you look at the Sabre water bottle,
嗯，在7分28秒的时候，如果你看那个赛博（Sabre）水瓶，

1257
00:55:48.580 --> 00:55:51.900
that was made by Clean Canteen.
那是Clean Canteen公司制造的。

1258
00:55:52.280 --> 00:55:52.700
Oh.
噢。

1259
00:55:52.880 --> 00:55:54.820
A little tidbit from Randy Cordray.
这是兰迪·科德雷（Randy Cordray）提供的一个小花絮。

1260
00:55:54.980 --> 00:55:59.200
And they also applied the logo that was designed by Henry Sane.
而且他们还印上了亨利·塞恩（Henry Sane）设计的标志。

1261
00:55:59.200 --> 00:56:05.240
I guess there were many, many variations of the Sabre logo that Greg and Paul had to choose from,
我想当时格雷格（Greg）和保罗（Paul）在很多很多个赛博标志的版本里做选择，

1262
00:56:05.320 --> 00:56:06.420
and that's the one they picked.
最后选了那一个。

1263
00:56:07.020 --> 00:56:07.700
But Jenna.
但是，珍娜（Jenna）。

1264
00:56:08.280 --> 00:56:08.640
Yeah.
嗯。

1265
00:56:08.860 --> 00:56:13.780
The whole time I was watching this scene, all I could remember was we did this.
我在看这一幕的时候，满脑子想的都是我们确实做过这件事。

1266
00:56:13.980 --> 00:56:15.060
We did this.
我们真的做过。

1267
00:56:15.200 --> 00:56:15.460
Yes.
没错。

1268
00:56:15.600 --> 00:56:21.100
Paul Lieberstein made us all drink out of these canteens.
保罗·利伯斯坦（Paul Lieberstein）让我们大家都用这种水壶喝水。

1269
00:56:21.300 --> 00:56:21.580
Yes.
是的。

1270
00:56:21.580 --> 00:56:26.200
And I was like, wait, I know I have something in my digital clutter about this.
我当时就想，等等，我记得我的数字杂物里有关于这件事的东西。

1271
00:56:26.420 --> 00:56:30.060
Some email saying that we were getting rid of plastic water bottles.
有封邮件说我们要弃用塑料水瓶了。

1272
00:56:30.200 --> 00:56:32.900
I knew I had something in my digital clutter about this.
我就知道我的数字杂物里有关于这个的内容。

1273
00:56:33.140 --> 00:56:33.460
Sam.
萨姆（Sam）。

1274
00:56:36.020 --> 00:56:37.260
Angela's digital clutter.
安吉拉（Angela）的数字杂物。

1275
00:56:38.940 --> 00:56:40.000
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1276
00:56:40.000 --> 00:56:45.780
So, Jenna, we all got an email during this time that there wouldn't be plastic water bottles on set.
所以，珍娜，我们当时都收到了一封邮件，说片场不再提供塑料水瓶了。

1277
00:56:45.960 --> 00:56:46.120
Yes, yes.
对，没错。

1278
00:56:46.140 --> 00:56:49.800
That we were all getting a stainless steel water bottle.
说我们每个人都会发一个不锈钢水瓶。

1279
00:56:49.940 --> 00:56:50.080
Yep.
没错。

1280
00:56:50.260 --> 00:56:51.720
That said Dunder Mifflin on it.
上面写着邓德·米夫林（Dunder Mifflin）。

1281
00:56:51.840 --> 00:56:52.000
Yep.
没错。

1282
00:56:52.160 --> 00:56:54.220
And we were going to refill them throughout the day.
而且我们要全天循环使用它们。

1283
00:56:54.680 --> 00:56:57.260
So, Jenna, you remembered so quickly it was Paul.
所以，珍娜，你记得这么快，是因为保罗。

1284
00:56:57.420 --> 00:57:03.000
I couldn't remember if it was Paul or Brent because I remember Brent was very much about being healthy and eco-friendly.
我记不清是保罗还是布伦特（Brent）了，因为我记得布伦特非常注重健康和环保。

1285
00:57:03.280 --> 00:57:03.460
Yes.
是的。

1286
00:57:03.640 --> 00:57:04.620
I texted Brent.
我给布伦特发了短信。

1287
00:57:04.760 --> 00:57:05.400
Brent, was this you?
布伦特，这是你做的吗？

1288
00:57:05.520 --> 00:57:07.560
He was like, no, I'm pretty sure it was Paul.
他说，不，我很确定是保罗。

1289
00:57:07.560 --> 00:57:12.180
So, then I emailed Paul and I said, Paul, I know we did this, right?
所以，我就给保罗发了邮件，我说，保罗，我知道我们做过这件事，对吧？

1290
00:57:12.300 --> 00:57:13.480
I found in my digital clutter.
我在我的数字杂物里找到了。

1291
00:57:13.620 --> 00:57:14.500
Was this your idea?
这是你的主意吗？

1292
00:57:14.700 --> 00:57:19.740
And was it also part of the inspiration for Gabe and his Saber water bottles?
这是否也是盖博（Gabe）和他的赛博水瓶的灵感来源之一？

1293
00:57:19.900 --> 00:57:21.440
And this is what Paul had to say.
这是保罗的回复。

1294
00:57:21.700 --> 00:57:25.600
Paul said, yes, I tried to get us to be plastic free.
保罗说，是的，我当时确实想让我们实现无塑料化。

1295
00:57:25.820 --> 00:57:27.100
It worked for a little while.
起初还挺管用的。

1296
00:57:27.280 --> 00:57:28.620
I remember that, too.
我也记得。

1297
00:57:28.640 --> 00:57:30.120
It was very short-lived.
但没持续多久。

1298
00:57:30.160 --> 00:57:30.540
I know.
我知道。

1299
00:57:30.540 --> 00:57:38.520
He said, as far as it being an intended storyline for Gabe, he doesn't have a clear memory that that was specifically a Gabe storyline.
他说，至于这是否是盖博的预设剧情，他记不清这是否专门是盖博的剧情线了。

1300
00:57:38.520 --> 00:57:43.640
But in general, so much of what was happening around us was inspiration for the show.
但总的来说，我们周围发生的很多事情都成为了节目的灵感来源。

1301
00:57:43.980 --> 00:57:44.540
All right.
好吧。

1302
00:57:44.760 --> 00:57:46.740
It was probably connected.
它可能当时是连着的。

1303
00:57:46.880 --> 00:57:49.180
But I was like, oh, my gosh, we did this.
但我当时想，天哪，我们竟然做了这个。

1304
00:57:49.380 --> 00:57:50.980
Do you know what I remembered?
你知道我记起了什么吗？

1305
00:57:51.320 --> 00:57:51.540
What?
什么？

1306
00:57:51.940 --> 00:57:53.440
Standing in line to refill it.
排队去续杯。

1307
00:57:53.580 --> 00:57:55.240
There literally was a line.
真的排起了长队。

1308
00:57:55.380 --> 00:57:55.660
Yes.
是的。

1309
00:57:55.660 --> 00:58:01.540
Well, you know, Paul told me that this was sort of a craze that was happening during this time.
嗯，你知道，保罗告诉我这在当时算是一种风潮。

1310
00:58:02.140 --> 00:58:05.100
Companies were really trying to limit plastic use.
各家公司都在极力限制塑料的使用。

1311
00:58:05.260 --> 00:58:08.260
And so he wanted us to be a part of that, you know?
所以他想让我们也参与其中，你懂的？

1312
00:58:08.260 --> 00:58:08.620
Yes.
是的。

1313
00:58:08.740 --> 00:58:10.540
I do think it's a great idea.
我觉得这确实是个好主意。

1314
00:58:11.180 --> 00:58:15.400
But I think you need more than one refill jug area.
但我认为你们需要不止一个续杯点。

1315
00:58:15.720 --> 00:58:17.460
That probably would have helped.
那可能会有帮助。

1316
00:58:17.520 --> 00:58:18.260
That would have helped.
那确实会有帮助。

1317
00:58:19.760 --> 00:58:23.540
Well, Michael has a talking head about all this where he says,
嗯，迈克尔有个关于这一切的访谈片段，他说，

1318
00:58:23.540 --> 00:58:29.760
okay, there's a small part of him that's excited about the new company, but 70% of him is water.
好吧，他内心有一小部分对新公司感到兴奋，但百分之七十的他都是水做的。

1319
00:58:30.040 --> 00:58:35.560
And at the end of this talking head, he says that he thinks these changes suck ball.
在这个访谈片段的最后，他说他觉得这些改变烂透了。

1320
00:58:36.520 --> 00:58:38.140
Because you know what he was going to say.
因为你知道他本来要说什么。

1321
00:58:38.440 --> 00:58:39.260
Sucks balls.
烂透了。

1322
00:58:39.460 --> 00:58:40.260
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1323
00:58:40.500 --> 00:58:45.480
I guess cutting off the end of Michael saying balls was an idea that John had.
我想把迈克尔说“烂透了”的后半部分剪掉是约翰的主意。

1324
00:58:45.640 --> 00:58:48.080
He came up with it in editing with Dave Rogers.
这是他在剪辑时和戴夫·罗杰斯一起想出来的。

1325
00:58:48.340 --> 00:58:50.460
And I love their take on this.
我很喜欢他们的处理方式。

1326
00:58:50.460 --> 00:58:54.560
So what they were saying was that, obviously, Michael completed his sentence.
他们想表达的是，很明显，迈克尔是把话说完了的。

1327
00:58:55.060 --> 00:59:03.240
But they imagined that when the documentary aired, that the documentarians would have left in all of the footage.
但他们设想当纪录片播出时，纪录片制作组会保留所有镜头。

1328
00:59:03.380 --> 00:59:07.820
But the network running the documentary would have to cut it off.
但播出纪录片的电视台必须把它剪掉。

1329
00:59:07.980 --> 00:59:08.520
Right.
没错。

1330
00:59:08.820 --> 00:59:11.000
Because of, you know, standards and practices.
因为，你知道，审查标准和规范。

1331
00:59:11.000 --> 00:59:18.840
And he said they based that on the amount of times that we had to cut things or change things because of standards and practices.
他说他们是基于我们因为审查标准和规范而不得不剪掉或修改内容的次数来构思的。

1332
00:59:18.840 --> 00:59:20.740
Every episode, probably.
大概每一集都要这样。

1333
00:59:20.960 --> 00:59:21.760
Very realistic.
非常写实。

1334
00:59:22.140 --> 00:59:26.980
Well, listen, Angela, you mentioned the line to fill their water bottles.
听着，安吉拉，你提到了他们排队接水。

1335
00:59:27.180 --> 00:59:30.740
And while Michael is in line, Toby's getting water and it runs out.
当迈克尔在排队时，托比正在接水，然后水没了。

1336
00:59:30.860 --> 00:59:32.400
Toby says we kicked it.
托比说我们把桶喝干了。

1337
00:59:32.520 --> 00:59:33.720
Which cracked me up.
这让我笑喷了。

1338
00:59:33.760 --> 00:59:34.280
Me too.
我也是。

1339
00:59:34.280 --> 00:59:37.160
I wrote it down at 8 minutes 45 seconds.
我在8分45秒的时候记下了这一点。

1340
00:59:37.740 --> 00:59:40.040
That's what you say when a keg runs out, right?
那是啤酒桶喝干时会说的话，对吧？

1341
00:59:40.160 --> 00:59:40.640
I know.
我知道。

1342
00:59:41.220 --> 00:59:43.360
Well, what does that tell us about Toby?
那么，这说明了托比的什么呢？

1343
00:59:43.360 --> 00:59:45.840
Well, I think, what does it tell us about Paul?
嗯，我觉得，这说明了保罗的什么呢？

1344
00:59:46.060 --> 00:59:50.800
Because I've bought a pony keg with Paul and we've kicked it.
因为我和保罗买过小桶啤酒，而且我们把它喝干过。

1345
00:59:51.020 --> 00:59:56.540
See, I would never use that language because I've never purchased a keg and I've never had a beer out of a keg.
你看，我永远不会用那种说法，因为我从没买过啤酒桶，也从没喝过桶装啤酒。

1346
00:59:56.860 --> 00:59:57.520
Oh, man.
天哪。

1347
00:59:57.680 --> 00:59:58.660
I'm not a beer person.
我不是个爱喝啤酒的人。

1348
00:59:58.960 --> 00:59:59.240
Listen.
听着。

1349
00:59:59.580 --> 01:00:04.140
Now, I'll do a flavored ale or a cider beer.
我现在会喝点调味艾尔啤酒或者苹果酒。

1350
01:00:04.420 --> 01:00:09.780
A really, really cold keg and like getting a beer out of a super cold keg.
那种超级冰的啤酒桶，从里面接一杯冰镇啤酒的感觉。

1351
01:00:09.780 --> 01:00:11.720
It's great, especially like on a hot day.
这感觉很棒，尤其是在炎热的天气里。

1352
01:00:11.980 --> 01:00:16.300
Maybe you put one, you know, at second base because you're playing softball with friends.
也许你可以在二垒放一个，你知道的，毕竟你是和朋友们打垒球。

1353
01:00:16.300 --> 01:00:22.780
And if you make it to second base, you get a beer and you get a little tooted while you're waiting to run into home plate.
如果你跑到了二垒，就能喝上一杯啤酒，在等候跑回本垒的时候还能稍微喝点儿。

1354
01:00:23.440 --> 01:00:25.820
That cold beer out of a keg.
从桶里接出来的那杯冰啤酒。

1355
01:00:25.920 --> 01:00:26.760
It's amazing.
简直太棒了。

1356
01:00:27.180 --> 01:00:28.940
I mean, that sounds miserable to me.
我是说，这听起来让我觉得很痛苦。

1357
01:00:29.140 --> 01:00:33.040
You drink some beer and then you have to run on your sloshy beer stomach.
你喝了啤酒，然后还得挺着装满啤酒的肚子去跑步。

1358
01:00:33.360 --> 01:00:37.720
Have you seen like co-ed softball, like with a group of friends?
你见过那种男女混合垒球赛吗，就是和一群朋友玩的那种？

1359
01:00:37.720 --> 01:00:39.200
This is not like real athleticism.
这可算不上真正的竞技运动。

1360
01:00:39.200 --> 01:00:42.060
You have lived part of life that I haven't lived.
你经历过我没经历过的人生。

1361
01:00:42.540 --> 01:00:44.180
You've had all these experiences.
你拥有过所有这些体验。

1362
01:00:44.400 --> 01:00:48.040
And to me, it's like you lived in a foreign land.
对我来说，就像是你生活在异国他乡一样。

1363
01:00:48.600 --> 01:00:48.840
What?
什么？

1364
01:00:49.040 --> 01:00:51.220
A foreign land of softball and beer?
垒球和啤酒的异国他乡？

1365
01:00:51.420 --> 01:00:51.780
Yeah.
没错。

1366
01:00:52.140 --> 01:00:55.440
I have no like frame of reference for that.
我对此完全没有概念。

1367
01:00:55.640 --> 01:00:57.960
I know you and Lee bond over this stuff all the time.
我知道你和李经常因为这些事打成一片。

1368
01:00:58.080 --> 01:00:59.160
Is this a Texas thing?
这是德州的特色吗？

1369
01:00:59.320 --> 01:01:00.920
I mean, I'm sure they're doing it in Missouri.
我是说，我相信密苏里州的人肯定也这么干。

1370
01:01:00.920 --> 01:01:01.880
Where was I?
我当时在哪儿呢？

1371
01:01:01.980 --> 01:01:03.660
What was I doing during this time?
那段时间我在干什么？

1372
01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:07.260
This was just like a hip young person out in the world.
这就像是那种在外面闯荡的时尚年轻人会做的事。

1373
01:01:07.260 --> 01:01:08.900
I've never been a hip young person.
我从来都不是什么时尚的年轻人。

1374
01:01:09.000 --> 01:01:09.620
Well, that's true.
嗯，确实。

1375
01:01:09.700 --> 01:01:12.620
I've been a 65-year-old woman since the day I was born.
我从出生那天起就像个65岁的老太太了。

1376
01:01:12.760 --> 01:01:13.240
It's true.
确实如此。

1377
01:01:13.240 --> 01:01:14.320
And I love you for it.
我爱你这一点。

1378
01:01:14.360 --> 01:01:14.960
Thank you, lady.
谢谢你，女士。

1379
01:01:15.240 --> 01:01:18.060
As I stare at your big fake flower that's on your lapel.
此时我正盯着你翻领上那朵巨大的假花。

1380
01:01:18.060 --> 01:01:19.360
I know it's not working.
我知道它坏了。

1381
01:01:19.500 --> 01:01:21.100
I know it's not working.
我知道它坏了。

1382
01:01:21.740 --> 01:01:27.900
I wore it in today because I wanted to prove to you that this cannot happen on our book launch tour.
我今天戴着它来，是因为我想向你证明，在我们的新书发布巡回活动上绝对不能出现这种情况。

1383
01:01:28.580 --> 01:01:29.320
It can't.
绝对不行。

1384
01:01:29.420 --> 01:01:29.920
Look at me.
看看我。

1385
01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:30.800
It's ridiculous.
这太荒唐了。

1386
01:01:31.260 --> 01:01:32.060
You never had to.
你根本没必要这么做。

1387
01:01:32.060 --> 01:01:33.720
Is water coming out of this flower?
这花里是在喷水吗？

1388
01:01:33.880 --> 01:01:34.660
Squirt, squirt.
滋，滋。

1389
01:01:34.760 --> 01:01:36.140
It's borderline clownish.
这简直跟小丑差不多了。

1390
01:01:36.140 --> 01:01:37.160
It can't happen.
这绝对不行。

1391
01:01:37.380 --> 01:01:39.160
You never had to prove it to me.
你从来都不需要向我证明什么。

1392
01:01:39.840 --> 01:01:41.640
I've known it from the beginning.
我从一开始就知道了。

1393
01:01:41.860 --> 01:01:44.060
Well, I needed to prove it to myself.
好吧，我是需要向自己证明一下。

1394
01:01:44.500 --> 01:01:45.260
All right.
好吧。

1395
01:01:45.460 --> 01:01:46.400
Where are we?
我们讲到哪儿了？

1396
01:01:46.880 --> 01:01:50.520
Well, Toby has just kicked the water cooler.
哦，托比刚刚踢了饮水机。

1397
01:01:50.760 --> 01:01:51.360
Oh, yes.
噢，对。

1398
01:01:51.480 --> 01:01:52.040
That's right.
没错。

1399
01:01:52.380 --> 01:01:54.540
Well, now Michael's going to confront Gabe.
好了，现在迈克尔要去和盖博对质了。

1400
01:01:54.900 --> 01:01:57.620
He's going to say, listen, I don't mean to seem ungrateful,
他会说，听着，我不是想显得不知好歹，

1401
01:01:57.620 --> 01:02:02.220
but I am really struggling to embrace some of these changes, such as all of them.
但我真的很难接受其中一些变化，比如全部的变化。

1402
01:02:03.880 --> 01:02:06.560
Gabe says it's kind of above his pay grade.
盖博说这超出了他的职权范围。

1403
01:02:06.800 --> 01:02:11.660
He can't really change any of the policies, but he'll see what he can do.
他无法真正改变任何政策，但他会看看能做些什么。

1404
01:02:12.080 --> 01:02:17.340
And now Pam and Jim are going to enter the daycare center.
现在帕姆和吉姆要进入日托中心了。

1405
01:02:17.340 --> 01:02:21.260
All of these scenes were absolutely delicious.
所有这些场景都绝对精彩。

1406
01:02:21.500 --> 01:02:23.560
I loved watching them.
我喜欢看这些片段。

1407
01:02:23.800 --> 01:02:25.840
We had a fan question from Alice R.
我们收到了一位来自意大利的粉丝爱丽丝·R的提问。

1408
01:02:25.940 --> 01:02:26.400
in Italy.
在意大利。

1409
01:02:26.660 --> 01:02:28.960
Where did you shoot the daycare scenes?
你们是在哪里拍摄日托中心场景的？

1410
01:02:29.120 --> 01:02:30.420
Was it a real daycare?
那是真的日托中心吗？

1411
01:02:30.720 --> 01:02:32.260
Did you make any changes?
你们做了什么改动吗？

1412
01:02:33.180 --> 01:02:35.040
Lady, did you recognize it?
女士，你认出它了吗？

1413
01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:35.960
No.
没有。

1414
01:02:36.580 --> 01:02:36.860
Okay.
好吧。

1415
01:02:36.900 --> 01:02:39.320
Well, it's called Sandbox Daycare.
嗯，它叫沙盒日托中心。

1416
01:02:39.400 --> 01:02:40.200
We made that up.
那是我们编出来的。

1417
01:02:40.400 --> 01:02:42.500
That's not even a real daycare in Scranton.
斯克兰顿根本没有那家日托中心。

1418
01:02:42.500 --> 01:02:47.200
And we shot this at Peekaboo Playland in Eagle Rock, California.
我们是在加州鹰岩的“躲猫猫游乐园”拍摄的。

1419
01:02:47.660 --> 01:02:50.080
Did you not take Isabel to Peekaboo Playland?
你没带伊莎贝尔去过“躲猫猫游乐园”吗？

1420
01:02:50.160 --> 01:02:52.460
Was that after she was a toddler?
那是她过了幼儿期之后的事吗？

1421
01:02:52.780 --> 01:02:55.280
This was all the rage when my kids were little.
我孩子小的时候，这里可是风靡一时。

1422
01:02:55.500 --> 01:02:56.960
Eagle Rock's far from me.
鹰岩离我太远了。

1423
01:02:57.060 --> 01:02:58.220
I guess that's true.
我想也是。

1424
01:02:58.540 --> 01:03:02.260
We had tons and tons of Playland-type places right by me,
我附近有很多很多这种游乐场，

1425
01:03:02.280 --> 01:03:04.160
so I never needed to venture this far.
所以我从没需要跑那么远。

1426
01:03:04.380 --> 01:03:07.240
Well, you know, when I did this episode, I didn't have kids.
嗯，你知道，拍这一集的时候我还没孩子。

1427
01:03:07.240 --> 01:03:10.260
But then when I was re-watching it, I was like, it's Peekaboo!
但后来重看的时候，我就想，那是“躲猫猫”！

1428
01:03:10.260 --> 01:03:11.760
Oh, it's Peekaboo Playland!
噢，那是“躲猫猫游乐园”！

1429
01:03:11.860 --> 01:03:15.320
I've spent so many days in this space!
我在这地方待过好多天！

1430
01:03:15.540 --> 01:03:17.160
See, the one by me is the coop.
你看，我附近那家叫“合作社”。

1431
01:03:17.400 --> 01:03:19.080
I spent tons of time at the coop.
我在“合作社”待过很长时间。

1432
01:03:19.260 --> 01:03:20.140
I've been to the coop.
我去过“合作社”。

1433
01:03:20.340 --> 01:03:20.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1434
01:03:21.080 --> 01:03:23.960
All right, so there's a big twirly slide in the middle.
好吧，中间有个巨大的旋转滑梯。

1435
01:03:24.260 --> 01:03:27.120
There's like a treehouse around the curly slide.
旋转滑梯周围有个树屋之类的东西。

1436
01:03:27.120 --> 01:03:28.680
It's the cutest dang thing.
那真是可爱得要命。

1437
01:03:29.260 --> 01:03:32.780
When we get there, Jim and Pam are totally charmed,
我们到那儿的时候，吉姆和帕姆完全被迷住了，

1438
01:03:34.100 --> 01:03:38.940
except Jim accidentally walks in on the daycare director
除了吉姆不小心撞见日托中心主任

1439
01:03:38.940 --> 01:03:41.100
who is using the little kitty toilet.
正在用那个小猫咪马桶。

1440
01:03:41.540 --> 01:03:43.620
Those toilets are so low to the ground.
那些马桶离地面太近了。

1441
01:03:43.980 --> 01:03:46.840
Well, they need to be because of the little children.
嗯，为了小孩子，它们必须得那么低。

1442
01:03:47.200 --> 01:03:49.480
I know, but seeing a grown man on it really did.
我知道，但看到一个成年男人坐在上面真的……

1443
01:03:50.300 --> 01:03:51.540
I was like, oh my God!
我当时心想，天哪！

1444
01:03:53.500 --> 01:03:57.280
John sent us in an audio clip of what it was like to shoot in the daycare.
约翰给我们发来了一段音频，讲述了在日托中心拍摄的感受。

1445
01:03:57.520 --> 01:03:58.540
Here's what he had to say.
听听他怎么说。

1446
01:03:59.180 --> 01:04:02.180
My other favorite memory from that episode
我对那一集另一个最深刻的记忆

1447
01:04:02.180 --> 01:04:05.340
was the interview at the daycare center.
就是日托中心的采访环节。

1448
01:04:05.540 --> 01:04:07.260
Jenna, as we've talked about many times,
珍娜，正如我们多次谈到的那样，

1449
01:04:07.400 --> 01:04:08.920
and I won't embarrass you on your own show,
我不会在你的节目上让你难堪，

1450
01:04:09.100 --> 01:04:10.500
I apologize, but not really.
我道歉，但其实也没那么抱歉。

1451
01:04:11.160 --> 01:04:14.380
Truly some of my favorite, favorite memories in all of my career
在我整个职业生涯中，我最最珍视的回忆之一，

1452
01:04:14.380 --> 01:04:16.180
were getting to do scenes with you, period.
就是能和你一起演对手戏，真的。

1453
01:04:16.780 --> 01:04:22.940
But especially those scenes where the two of us were sort of stuck in it together,
尤其是那些我们俩被困在一起的场景，

1454
01:04:23.120 --> 01:04:25.560
that we were both in something that we had to get out of together.
我们必须共同面对困境，设法脱身。

1455
01:04:25.560 --> 01:04:28.240
I remember very specifically your line reading
我特别记得你当时的那句台词，

1456
01:04:28.240 --> 01:04:32.260
when I came out from seeing Jerry in the bathroom.
就是我从洗手间看到杰瑞出来之后。

1457
01:04:32.860 --> 01:04:34.840
And I said, I just saw someone in the bathroom.
我说，我刚在洗手间看到个人。

1458
01:04:35.120 --> 01:04:38.460
And you very earnestly ask, who was it?
然后你非常认真地问，是谁？

1459
01:04:38.580 --> 01:04:39.320
Who was it?
是谁？

1460
01:04:39.380 --> 01:04:42.260
And then you quickly digress as your brain realizes,
紧接着你的大脑反应过来，迅速转了话题，

1461
01:04:42.520 --> 01:04:44.960
oh, it was definitely the guy that we're about to interview.
噢，那肯定就是我们要去面试的那个人。

1462
01:04:45.140 --> 01:04:47.120
And your line reading of who was it?
你那句“是谁？”，

1463
01:04:47.180 --> 01:04:47.660
Who was it?
“是谁？”，

1464
01:04:47.780 --> 01:04:49.520
Was it the guy who's going to interview us?
是那个要面试我们的人吗？

1465
01:04:49.620 --> 01:04:51.880
It was so funny.
真的太搞笑了。

1466
01:04:51.880 --> 01:04:56.580
And I don't know that I had a good enough take of my reaction to you.
我不知道我当时对你的反应有没有拍出好的镜头。

1467
01:04:56.760 --> 01:04:59.900
In fact, do I physically bail out after you say that to me?
事实上，你跟我说完那句话后，我是不是直接笑场跑掉了？

1468
01:05:00.600 --> 01:05:02.460
Man, that really made me laugh.
天哪，那真的把我逗乐了。

1469
01:05:02.620 --> 01:05:05.480
I seem to remember going through, I don't know,
我记得我好像拍了，不知道，

1470
01:05:05.680 --> 01:05:09.360
10, 12 takes of just not being able to keep it together.
十到十二条，就是因为一直憋不住笑。

1471
01:05:09.680 --> 01:05:13.060
That was a total GiggleFest day for me.
那天对我来说简直就是一场“笑场狂欢”。

1472
01:05:13.180 --> 01:05:16.640
You were always more professional, but I was in full GiggleFest mode.
你总是更专业一些，但我当时完全处于“笑场狂欢”模式。

1473
01:05:16.920 --> 01:05:19.700
And shout out to my friend, Joey Slotnick, who played Jerry.
还要特别提一下我的朋友乔伊·斯洛特尼克，他饰演了杰瑞。

1474
01:05:19.700 --> 01:05:21.660
I was so excited to get him on the show.
我当时特别兴奋能请他来客串。

1475
01:05:21.860 --> 01:05:23.480
And he absolutely crushed it.
他演得简直绝了。

1476
01:05:23.720 --> 01:05:29.000
That gesture he does in the bathroom where he silently raises his hand.
他在洗手间里那个默默举手的动作。

1477
01:05:29.420 --> 01:05:33.580
But there is no, there is nothing said between the two people.
两人之间什么话都没说。

1478
01:05:34.100 --> 01:05:37.600
Just utter shame and embarrassment and guilt.
只有满屏的羞耻、尴尬和愧疚。

1479
01:05:37.860 --> 01:05:39.360
He was so great on that show.
他在那集里表现得太棒了。

1480
01:05:39.480 --> 01:05:42.680
And I just remember yet again, just getting to watch those scenes
我记得当时又一次，能看着那些场景，

1481
01:05:42.680 --> 01:05:44.160
and not have to give any notes.
完全不需要给出任何指导意见。

1482
01:05:45.140 --> 01:05:50.060
All right, so I just have to say, I totally remember that.
好吧，我必须得说，我完全记得那一幕。

1483
01:05:50.200 --> 01:05:53.480
Yes, John, you do physically bail out of the scene.
没错，约翰，你确实在那个场景里笑场跑掉了。

1484
01:05:53.980 --> 01:05:55.540
But also, you know what?
但还有，你知道吗？

1485
01:05:55.620 --> 01:05:59.340
I really appreciate him saying that he liked shooting these scenes with me
我真的很感激他说喜欢和我拍这些戏，

1486
01:05:59.340 --> 01:06:04.420
because I think there's often a lot written about our romantic chemistry on screen.
因为我觉得大家往往更关注我们在银幕上的浪漫化学反应。

1487
01:06:04.700 --> 01:06:08.280
But we had a really special comedic chemistry together.
但我们之间其实有一种非常特别的喜剧化学反应。

1488
01:06:08.280 --> 01:06:11.900
And I feel like this storyline really highlights that.
我觉得这条故事线很好地突显了这一点。

1489
01:06:12.060 --> 01:06:14.200
We were great partners all around.
我们在各方面都是很棒的搭档。

1490
01:06:14.520 --> 01:06:15.360
I agree.
我同意。

1491
01:06:15.360 --> 01:06:20.440
And I loved what John said about when you guys were both in a sticky situation together.
我很喜欢约翰说的，关于你们俩陷入困境时的那种默契。

1492
01:06:21.000 --> 01:06:22.640
Yes, I loved it.
是的，我也很喜欢。

1493
01:06:23.020 --> 01:06:27.780
And, you know, John mentioned Jerry, the daycare director, was played by Joey Slotnick.
而且，约翰提到了杰瑞，那个托儿所主管，是由乔伊·斯洛特尼克扮演的。

1494
01:06:27.880 --> 01:06:30.340
He was a really good friend of John's.
他是约翰很好的朋友。

1495
01:06:30.560 --> 01:06:34.040
He had also been in John's movie, Brief Interviews with Hideous Men.
他也出演过约翰执导的电影《男人众生相》。

1496
01:06:34.040 --> 01:06:38.440
But Joey had actually auditioned for this part through Alison Jones.
但其实乔伊是通过艾莉森·琼斯试镜得到这个角色的。

1497
01:06:38.740 --> 01:06:41.360
I guess he'd auditioned for other roles on the show.
我想他之前也为剧里的其他角色试过镜。

1498
01:06:41.640 --> 01:06:45.060
And when this role came up, she thought of him.
当这个角色出现时，她就想到了他。

1499
01:06:45.200 --> 01:06:46.540
And she knew he was John's friend.
而且她也知道他是约翰的朋友。

1500
01:06:47.160 --> 01:06:53.980
But you might recognize Joey from the TV shows Alias, Boston Public, The Single Guy, or Nip Tuck.
不过你可能在《双面女间谍》、《波士顿公立学校》、《单身汉》或《整容室》这些剧里见过乔伊。

1501
01:06:54.080 --> 01:06:57.940
He was also in the movies Twister and The Secret Life of Walter Mitty,
他还出演过电影《龙卷风》和《白日梦想家》，

1502
01:06:58.280 --> 01:07:01.680
which, by the way, is one of my favorite movies directed by Ben Stiller.
顺便说一下，那是我最喜欢的本·斯蒂勒执导的电影之一。

1503
01:07:01.680 --> 01:07:04.880
Well, I met Joey years ago when I first came to Los Angeles.
嗯，我多年前刚来洛杉矶时就认识乔伊了。

1504
01:07:04.880 --> 01:07:09.380
My friend got me a job just for one season being a stand-in on The Single Guy.
我朋友帮我找了份工作，在《单身汉》剧组当了一季的替身演员。

1505
01:07:09.720 --> 01:07:11.560
I didn't know you were a stand-in.
我不知道你还当过替身演员。

1506
01:07:11.700 --> 01:07:13.320
Yeah, just for one season.
是啊，就那一季。

1507
01:07:13.560 --> 01:07:13.820
Still.
那也很厉害了。

1508
01:07:14.100 --> 01:07:15.120
It was so cool.
真的很酷。

1509
01:07:15.300 --> 01:07:17.980
What a great way to learn the ins and outs of a four-camera show.
这是学习四机位拍摄流程的绝佳方式。

1510
01:07:18.200 --> 01:07:18.640
Yes.
没错。

1511
01:07:18.780 --> 01:07:22.520
You know, I did background work for years when I first came out.
你知道，我刚入行时也做了好几年的背景演员。

1512
01:07:22.640 --> 01:07:22.900
Same.
我也是。

1513
01:07:23.200 --> 01:07:27.380
A great way to just sit on a set and observe how it works.
这是坐在片场观察拍摄运作的绝佳方式。

1514
01:07:27.380 --> 01:07:32.980
So by the time I finally booked a role and I had a line, I was like, oh, I know the flow.
所以当我终于接到一个有台词的角色时，我就想，噢，我了解整个流程。

1515
01:07:33.160 --> 01:07:34.600
Like, I know some of the language.
比如，我懂一些行话。

1516
01:07:34.880 --> 01:07:35.820
I know this world.
我熟悉这个世界。

1517
01:07:36.060 --> 01:07:39.860
And in four-camera stand-ins walk through the role while they're lighting.
在四机位拍摄中，替身演员会在灯光师布光时走位。

1518
01:07:40.120 --> 01:07:41.800
They say the lines that go to the mark.
他们会念出台词并走到标记点。

1519
01:07:41.980 --> 01:07:43.460
It was such a great education.
那真是一次很棒的学习经历。

1520
01:07:43.460 --> 01:07:45.480
And Joey was so nice to everyone.
而且乔伊对每个人都特别好。

1521
01:07:45.620 --> 01:07:46.620
That's my memory of him.
这就是我对他的印象。

1522
01:07:46.860 --> 01:07:51.780
Well, we got some mail asking, why aren't there any kids at this daycare?
嗯，我们收到了一些邮件问，为什么这家托儿所里没有孩子？

1523
01:07:52.240 --> 01:07:52.680
Right.
对。

1524
01:07:52.680 --> 01:07:54.540
Well, there actually were.
其实是有的。

1525
01:07:54.920 --> 01:08:00.560
The kids were staged doing a little story time, but they were over to the side.
孩子们当时在旁边排练讲故事的环节，只是在侧面。

1526
01:08:00.760 --> 01:08:06.980
So when Pam and Jim arrive, there was like a mini scene of the kids doing story time.
所以当帕姆和吉姆到达时，有一个孩子们讲故事的小场景。

1527
01:08:07.180 --> 01:08:09.180
And Pam and Jim have a little aww moment.
帕姆和吉姆还流露出了那种“好可爱”的温馨时刻。

1528
01:08:09.860 --> 01:08:16.080
And then John actually directed me when he was going to walk to the bathroom to go up to the
约翰当时还指导我，说等他要去洗手间的时候，让我走到

1529
01:08:16.080 --> 01:08:21.620
little tea set and just be like pretending like I was a kid doing tea and I was like so
那套小茶具旁，假装自己是个在玩过家家的小孩，我当时觉得

1530
01:08:21.620 --> 01:08:22.140
charmed.
太迷人了。

1531
01:08:22.580 --> 01:08:28.380
And Jen shared that they really liked just following me and John rather than cutting away
珍也分享说，他们其实更喜欢一直跟着我和约翰拍，而不是切走镜头

1532
01:08:28.380 --> 01:08:29.400
and showing the kids.
去拍那些孩子。

1533
01:08:29.560 --> 01:08:35.020
So they actually edited out that story time bit for time because they just liked staying
所以为了节省时间，他们剪掉了讲故事的那部分，因为他们更喜欢保留

1534
01:08:35.020 --> 01:08:37.860
with our enthusiasm over the daycare center.
我们对托儿所那种兴奋的状态。

1535
01:08:38.060 --> 01:08:38.400
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1536
01:08:38.540 --> 01:08:38.940
I agree.
我同意。

1537
01:08:39.180 --> 01:08:41.760
You guys are just so delighted to be new parents.
你们俩作为新手父母看起来真的太开心了。

1538
01:08:41.760 --> 01:08:45.080
And I loved the line when Jim says, oh, cubbies.
我很喜欢吉姆说的那句台词，噢，储物格。

1539
01:08:45.220 --> 01:08:46.440
I forgot about cubbies.
我都忘了还有储物格这回事了。

1540
01:08:46.540 --> 01:08:46.840
Yes.
是啊。

1541
01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:49.300
Because that's really how it is when you have kids.
因为当你有了孩子，现实确实就是这样。

1542
01:08:49.520 --> 01:08:51.840
All of these memories come back to you.
所有的记忆都会涌上心头。

1543
01:08:51.940 --> 01:08:52.540
It's true.
确实如此。

1544
01:08:53.160 --> 01:08:58.440
Well, right after this Jim and Pam scene at the daycare would have been the second part
嗯，在托儿所这场吉姆和帕姆的戏之后，紧接着应该是

1545
01:08:58.440 --> 01:08:59.780
of this accounting runner.
会计组那条副线剧情的第二部分。

1546
01:09:00.040 --> 01:09:03.020
The one where Angela's giving fake work to Kevin?
就是安吉拉给凯文布置假工作的那段吗？

1547
01:09:03.220 --> 01:09:03.460
Yes.
没错。

1548
01:09:03.460 --> 01:09:04.180
I love it.
